{"id":222012970547482,"type":"song","name":"Funky New Year","artist":"The Eagles","year":1978,"weight":10,"info":{"img":null},"artist_ref":{"id":106115726467187,"name":"The Eagles","info":{"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/178be204025c8d38a72113564b647baf/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg"}},"labels":[],"genres":[],"lists":[],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This Eagles original song served as the flip side to their 1978 single, \"Please Come Home for Christmas.\" Don Henley stated that the band felt more comfortable writing an original song about New Year's hangovers, as it was \"in their wheelhouse,\" compared to composing an original Christmas song. \"Don Henley said that the band knew a lot more about being hung over on New Year's. So writing an original about that felt a little more like it was in their wheelhouse than writing an original Christmas song.\"","year":1978,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 52 - 70s Christmas Music","url":"https://www.ftr70.com/"},{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 52 - 70s Christmas Music","url":null}]}],"book_tracks":[],"others":[{"id":147132100610675,"type":"album","name":"Hotel California","year":1976,"weight":38},{"id":176138389135991,"type":"song","name":"One of These Nights","year":1975,"weight":28},{"id":170101285485673,"type":"album","name":"Desperado","year":1972,"weight":28},{"id":174811107218091,"type":"album","name":"One of These Nights","year":1975,"weight":23},{"id":135134731009764,"type":"song","name":"Lyin' Eyes","year":1976,"weight":21},{"id":59847593244658,"type":"album","name":"Eagles","year":1972,"weight":20},{"id":117234253472183,"type":"song","name":"Hotel California","year":1977,"weight":17},{"id":107237987564206,"type":"album","name":"The Long Run","year":1979,"weight":16},{"id":55222976077620,"type":"album","name":"On the Border","year":1974,"weight":16},{"id":26937411688903,"type":"song","name":"Take It to the Limit","year":